    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection to match the new specification. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2).\n\n### Changes\n\n**`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 now returns the 64-char lower-case hex SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (via `Sha256Hex.lowerHex` and `Soundex.encode`), replacing the former plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`. The telephone and email are already normalized/lower-cased at the point this is computed in the create pipeline.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.isPossibleDuplicateOf(...)`** \u2014 the soft-match now triggers when the identity keys **differ** but **postcode** and **soundex(lastName)** match (previously: same postcode + case-insensitive lastName + different telephone). Added the `Soundex` import.\n\n**Behavioural consequences that fall out of these two changes:**\n- Two owners with the same lastName + postcode but **different telephones** now produce different identity keys \u2192 no 409; instead they're flagged as a soft match (same postcode + soundex, differing key).\n- The identity key no longer contains `householdId`, so the single identity-key check is the only duplicate rule. The `householdId` is still computed and used for household size/membership-level capping. (There was no active household-duplicate 409 to remove \u2014 `HouseholdDuplicateException` was already never thrown.)\n- The email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeOwnerFields`), and soft-deleted owners are still ignored (via `existingOwners()`) \u2014 both unchanged.\n\n**Docs/comments** \u2014 updated the now-inaccurate Javadoc/comments in `Owner`, `OwnerRestControllerV1` (create pipeline, `rejectWhenIdentityInUse`, `applyHouseholdMembership`, `rejectDisallowedOwnerCreation`), and the `identityKey` / `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` descriptions and example in `openapi.yml`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests now pass: `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (asserts the returned key matches `[0-9a-f]{64}`) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical telephone/email/lastName \u2192 409).",
